\pard\tx1140\tx2300\tx3440\tx4600\tx5760\tx6900\tx8060\tx9200\tx10360\tx11520\f0\b\i0\ul0\fs36 NeXTspim\

\f1\b0\fs24 \

\f2 I developed NeXTspim under NeXTstep 2.1 on black hardware.  I do not know whether or not it will compile on other platforms or with a newer verison of the OS.\
\
To make NeXTspim, just use the existing makefile, or work through Interface Builder.  If you do "make install" to create a file package, you must copy trap.handler into that package so that NeXTspim can find it.\

\f1 \

\f2\b\fs28 Changes to existing code:\

\b0\fs24 The function 
\f1 write-output
\f2  no longer has the first 
\f1 int
\f2  argument to specify the window.  All output will go to the Messages window.   
\f1 mips-syscall.c
\f2  and 
\f1 mem.c
\f2  were changed to reflect this.\
\
A line was commented out in 
\f1 mem.c
\f2  to prevent the memory-mapped I/O routines from doubling the characters on the screen.  Since NeXTspim uses a ConsoleText object, the characters are automatically placed.\
\
The 
\f1 initialize_world
\f2  function in 
\f1 spim-util.c
\f2  has been modified to include the path of the executable in the filename for the default trap handler.  This is important, since the working directory of an executable launched from the File Viewer is the user's home directory, not the directory where the executable is.\
\

